p.src:
A massless particle cannot be brought to rest, but a massive particle can. At rest $k=0$, so the wavefunction has no spatial variation and $\omega=\beta m.$ The differential equation reduces to $i\frac{d\Psi}{dt}=m\beta\Psi.$ In components, $\begin{aligned}
i\dot{\psi}_R&=m\psi_L,\\
i\dot{\psi}_L&=m\psi_R.\end{aligned}$ Both off-diagonal entries of $\beta$ are $+1$, so there is no extra minus sign in either of these equations.

